 a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -8 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nSince $A∼B,$ the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the equation $Bx=0,$ which corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that the only solution of $Ax=0$ is $x=0.$ So, $\\text{Null}(A)={0},$ which means that the basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ is the empty set, i.e., $B={\\,}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34523/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cba14b5-62f7-5fbe-beb1-9b1511305cc6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34523"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75017/selection/771df565adae2583f3c3f45636a1fb9a4b22547b5daa8c6c5e67434ea9894c36" :answer/id #uuid "729ecde4-4d1e-52aa-a059-dec29ab49c77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75017/selection/7b6b8e157076c7c747face171aff22f1a37de43e0091d7611d1418b150440a42" :answer/id #uuid "a050668e-1a94-5bfa-9953-04713916cd10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75017/selection/6dcdacfe6250159f1c19254ba9ed8d031f6f9f7fab290de1175e198c6e82f4ac" :answer/id #uuid "92419916-93ed-5ae9-9d12-4fbc37d7fbe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75017/selection/8e11c1a124ff0cefb0c6ed76c35c6ad3ffbc360f47ca69a88686ffe16f