begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that the only solution of $Ax=0$ is $x=0.$ So, $\\text{Null}(A)={0},$ which means that the basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ is the empty set, i.e., $B={\\,}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75017/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cba14b5-62f7-5fbe-beb1-9b1511305cc6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75017"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120276 :question/answer-fields 17592186118131] {:db/id "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" :answer/id #uuid "46528645-737a-5f30-b188-a4a35aa7ebfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/47ca9b38dee9e032667a6d1f10eb87228e6fa93da8cb157c8506929d2e22ee67" :answer/id #uuid "083b46ee-c8bd-537d-a9ef-1b54ff3bc9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={\\,}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/18c831a9c9a8e55c9e12adecf0be12ef2c56045e943a7c4f5d00a2825b893d23" :answer/id #uuid "d8dcd965-7a76-555f-b9fa-5e75154d241f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/d7cb3336f47360de323b5374f2dfd8b97debdb73b2743839dc6878801641061e" :answer/id #uuid "8ad6592d-cca3-534d-b145-81c8193008a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/8e0362e18d0bb33cd10caed891eb4d316cbe4677b70f202cac2c8050532ffb79" :answer/id #uuid "00ca7173-ddbc-5572-b57f-c7f1f92403fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf" :answer-field/id #uuid "a3b9bf28-a189-505a-aeec-7e7d556ef827" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" :answer-field/choices ["q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/eddc584b31d4a80179e9498da1aeab49ea2c84f0426c04a753bb5632fe5ce44f" "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/47ca9b38dee9e032667a6d1f10eb87228e6fa93da8cb157c8506929d2e22ee67" "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/18c831a9c9a8e55c9e12adecf0be12ef2c56045e943a7c4f5d00a2825b893d23" "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/d7cb3336f47360de323b5374f2dfd8b97debdb73b2743839dc6878801641061e" "q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf/8e0362e18d0bb33cd10caed891eb4d316cbe4677b70f202cac2c8050532ffb79"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34522"] :question/problem "The matrices $A$ and $B$ are given below. Given that $A$ is row equivalent to $B$, then find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nSince $A∼B,$ the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the equation $Bx=0,$ which corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=0,$ where ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34522/selection/ma-v1/d17c48edf1ed85733ba2125ca65b34c6a68c84025eb7f4a0902f3583f769e4bf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-111509/selection/8e11c1a124ff0cefb0c6ed76c35c6ad3ffbc360f47ca69a88686ffe16f4e6411" :answer/id #uuid "a34337a7-23a4-58bb-bec5-459558c241df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111509/selection/dc1d9aef9cd36dab6f357387961be9892b9c24f2009c3ee352fcc703f95be69e" :answer/id #uuid "186c0842-a763-5d45-9340-9ae3e710152c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111509/selection/47ca9b38dee9e032667a6d1f10eb87228e6fa93da8cb157c8506929d2e22ee67" :answer/id #uuid "7e5756ad-a87c-54dc-89d3-a3a955ffd00a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={\\,}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111509/selection/15aa5158a63ae21ae09e9dece186da3669d10ceb90ec12310dde180f2a81dc1d" :answer/id #uuid "23b208d7-6812-5895-843a-821549bdfb07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111509/selection/d44d27fac97d5be9fbbd535a842bdce69cb7b3cdbd1f3d77aefdb9dac18cdb33" :answer/id #uuid "3f0a08fd-a78a-51e6-8bd7-adde63467734" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111509/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "791a41f7-4eef-5728-8d11-61bfc14eb768" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111509/selection/15aa5158a63ae21ae09e9dece186da3669d10ceb90ec12310dde180f2a81dc1d" :answer-field/choices ["q-111509/selection/8e11c1a124ff0cefb0c6ed76c35c6ad3ffbc360f47ca69a88686ffe16f4e6411" "q-111509/selection/dc1d9aef9cd36dab6f357387961be9892b9c24f2009c3ee352fcc703f95be69e" "q-111509/selection/47ca9b38dee9e032667a6d1f10eb87228e6fa93da8cb157c8506929d2e22ee67" "q-111509/selection/15aa5158a63ae21ae09e9dece186da3669d10ceb90ec12310dde180f2a81dc1d" "q-111509/selection/d44d27fac97d5be9fbbd535a842bdce69cb7b3cdbd1f3d77aefdb9dac18cdb33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111509" :question/id #uuid "7ecba0a9-69d1-5f64-879a-c0fef7364a6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-111509" :question/problem "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$, find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=0$ is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe general solution is ${x}_{1}=-{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=0,$ where ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. Therefore, if $x\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThis implies that \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nis a basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ since it is a linearly independent set and its vectors generate $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111509/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0fd5a675-c692-505e-900b-d7500fb7c653"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111509"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-34422/selection/e5402976e3454c3d42a7c892015d52b6504db08e26b9754c64ebeccd6f821bf7" :answer/id #uuid "eec0c845-0c94-51bb-925a-1994d88c6c87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34422/selection/f639f150287a95bee3e517379c75de510a4cd9e3bc359eed9d03a9e594f824fc" :answer/id #uuid "bd02b7bf-f7ef-5728-848f-639185aeeb5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34422/selection/28b4bae639790da58210f04cd074f081ca0602cd8cac01fc317c1b731615c933" :answer/id #uuid "0097398b-e456-50d4-a8a1-10f85c798cee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\